    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "`python -m app.server --http` now works. It serves the inventory server over Streamable HTTP at `/mcp` and keeps running until the process is stopped.\n\n**The change** (`app/server.py:28`):\n\n```python\ndef serve_http(host: str, port: int) -> None:\n    build_server().run(\"streamable-http\", host=host, port=port)\n```\n\nThe pinned `mcp==2.2.0` already has this transport built in. `/mcp` is its default path, and it uses uvicorn, which is already installed. I didn't add or change any dependencies, and stdio mode is untouched.\n\n**Checks I ran:**\n- `pytest -q`: 2 passed.\n- I started `python -m app.server --http --port 8765` and sent it an MCP `initialize` request at `http://127.0.0.1:8765/mcp`. It answered 200 with the inventory server's details and was still running afterwards.\n\n**Two things to know:**\n- **Remote access needs `--host 0.0.0.0` (or a specific interface).** The default is `127.0.0.1`, so other machines can't connect without it. On localhost the library also turns on DNS-rebinding protection, and it doesn't do that on other addresses. There's no authentication either way, so only expose it on a network you trust.\n- **Please delete `_smoke.py` from the project root.** It's the temporary smoke-test script, and my request to remove it needed approval that wasn't given."
  },
